# MR (SOFT, card M only): the one-hour mesh-read probe that decides MR (one mesh-level verify readback) and 2a (the joined quad reads) of the fusion plan (optimisation/ttnn-op/mr_probe). It times, on the same data, the served loop (every chip's ids part, then every chip's values part), two mesh-level reads, ONE joined
# word tensor (the packed (column << 16) | bits layout) read once, and a non-blocking per-chip read with one synchronise; plus the same loop and mesh read on a 32 x 32 tile (the quad draft's output size class). It is host-only code; nothing is computed on the device.
# ONE CARD SEES ONE CHIP: the verdict line reads INCONCLUSIVE-SINGLE-CHIP by construction, and what it measures is the floor L of one read and the per-call overhead of the mesh composer. The decision needs a quad run: the four-chip cost of the served loop is the reads_ms field of the [PACKED-HOSTGAP-VERIFY] lines the w2 arms already log
# (QWEN_FAST_TP4_HOSTGAP_LOG=1), read from T2 or P1 and put beside this report's floor (the served loop at four chips is about 8 L), the mesh arm's overhead and the word arm. If a multi-chip container is ever given to the harness (it opens a mesh over every device it sees) the verdict is GO / MESH-ONLY / NO-GO (a quarter or more saved).
# READ: the 'MR_PROBE verdict=...' line, the last stdout line (one JSON object, kind mr-probe), any arm's error (an arm whose API is missing is skipped, not fatal). Duration (estimate): 60 min (the reads are minutes; the rest is the attach). Soft.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/w2 window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/w2 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the card is resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# CARD M ONLY, BEFORE ANY QUAD JOB: the cardm step runs one board; it never runs while a quad step holds the cards, and the harness refuses while anything else can reach the board.
# The harness's container turns the image's C2 boot hook off (QWEN_C2_SERVING=0) and unsets the baked four-card mesh descriptor (env -u TT_MESH_GRAPH_DESC_PATH); the workflow's
# cardm step waits for other CI's buildx builders instead of refusing the window. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w2-1 is the image B0 built (a harness mounts this checkout's scripts, so any current C2 image carries the runtime it needs).
C2_CARDS=pair
C2_ACTIONS=cardm
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w2-1
C2_CARDM_HARNESS=optimisation/ttnn-op/mr_probe/run_card_m.sh
C2_CARDM_ENV=IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w2-1
